    "equation": "Yu et al. (2024), Equations 1 and 4-8: BM3 300 K reference isotherm plus integrated constant-q Mie-Gruneisen-Debye thermal pressure"
   },
   "notes": "Preferred thermal parameterization from Table 1: a 300 K third-order Birch-Murnaghan reference isotherm plus quasi-harmonic Mie-Gruneisen-Debye thermal pressure. Equations 7-8 specify gamma=gamma0(V/V0)^q and theta=theta0*exp[-(gamma-gamma0)/q], which is Peritheos's integrated_gruneisen law, not the Fei et al. variable-exponent law used for the Pt calibrant. The source conventional-cell volumes are converted internally to molar volume using Z=6, while the public API remains in A^3 per conventional hexagonal cell. The paper also reports a separate high-temperature BM3 reference-state fit with alpha0, alpha1, and dK/dT; it is not represented here because the preferred MGD model is explicitly described as more reliable for extrapolation and is used in the downstream mantle calculations. The publication does not report the regression weights, residual definition, coefficient covariance, or confidence convention for parenthetical parameter errors. An independent unweighted pressure-residual refit is therefore a transparent reproduction diagnostic rather than a claim to duplicate the unpublished regression protocol.",
